# Software Development Paradigms: Comparing C and Python 🚀


**Note:** This project documentation was made by using   "Google Docs".



## 📄 Project Highlights
This project breaks down the core differences between the two languages using the "Recipe vs. The Factory" analogy. 

### ⚙️ C (The Procedural Paradigm)
- **Approach:** Uses a procedural, sequential method.
- **Execution:** It is a compiled language that translates the entire program into machine code.
- **Performance:** Offers blazing speed because it is extremely close to the hardware.
- **Memory & Structure:** Relies on manual memory allocation and global variables.

### 🐍 Python (The Object-Oriented Paradigm)
- **Approach:** Uses an object-oriented and structured strategy.
- **Execution:** It is an interpreted language.
- **Scalability:** Helps keep large projects organized and prevents them from turning into a "spaghetti" mess of code..
